<title>JAPAN: Green Cross names new president.</title>
<headline>Green Cross names new president.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese drug maker Green Cross Corp on Thursday named Kazunari Doi as its president in place of Takehiko Kawano, who was arrested earlier this month.</p>
<p>Kawano was arrested on suspicion of professional negligence resulting in death for his role in the sale of HIV-contaminated blood products. His two predecessors have also been arrested on the same charge.</p>
<p>Doi, the new president, is a former vice president who was in charge of overseas operations for most of his years as an executive for the firm.</p>
</text>
